Steps to Deploy Gemini Temperature Agent on AWS EC2

--------------------------------------------------------
 Create EC2 Instance

Go to AWS Console → EC2 → Launch Instance

Choose AWS Linux or Ubunut 

Instance type: t2.medium (recommended)

Storage: 8–16 GB

Add Security Group rules:

SSH (22) → Your IP

Custom TCP (8501) → 0.0.0.0/0

--- Connect to EC2
ssh -i your-key.pem ec2-user@<EC2-PUBLIC-IP>

--- Update & Install Dependencies

Update packages

Install python3, pip, git, virtualenv

--- Create Project Directory
mkdir ~/gemini_temperature_agent
cd ~/gemini_temperature_agent

--- Setup Virtual Environment

Create a Python virtual environment

Activate the environment

--- Create Required Files

Inside the project folder, create these files:

requirements.txt → contains required Python packages

app.py → main Streamlit app code


--- Install Python Packages
pip install -r requirements.txt

--- Get Gemini API Key
Google AI Studio--    https://aistudio.google.com/

Sign in with your Google account

Create a new API key

Copy the key

---- Configure API Key on EC2
export GEMINI_API_KEY="your-api-key-here"


To persist after reboot:

echo 'export GEMINI_API_KEY="your-api-key-here"' >> ~/.bashrc
source ~/.bashrc


-----Add Swap (if using small instance)

Create a 2GB swap file

Enable it and persist in /etc/fstab

----Run Streamlit App

Test run in foreground:

streamlit run app.py --server.port 8501 --server.address 0.0.0.0


----Access the App

Open in browser:

http://<EC2-PUBLIC-IP>:8501

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Output should be the webbrowser page with "Gemini Temperature agent"


